  "recommendation": {
    "word": "hold",
    "why": "The shipped flag keeps the panel layer at the final size on every morph frame, shows every child where the original shows it (Lean paint_eq, inset_width_eq) and passes the breakpoint gate on both engines. The measured counts belong to a first design with a wrapper element, which failed the gate; they show no difference from the base beyond the pass-to-pass spread, which is expected since layout inputs are unchanged, and the Simulator has no GPU and logs no surface allocations. The final design has no base-against-flag run yet, and the nav resize and the column tracks still change size on every frame. Hold until the final design is measured on a lane with a real GPU."
  }
